  "goodToKnow": "Der Wasserstoff is hydrogen. German translated its scientific name (hydrogen, from Greek water-maker) as water substance. It's a big part of Germany's energy plans: grüner Wasserstoff, made with renewable electricity, is meant to replace natural gas in industry. In 2018, Lower Saxony launched the world's first passenger trains running on Wasserstoff. Similar element names: Sauerstoff (oxygen), Stickstoff (nitrogen), Kohlenstoff (carbon)."
